Responsibilities
The different projects you will work on will include the following tasks:
Participate in daily scrum, sprint planning, sprint review and retrospective meetings;
Develop new functionalities and validate their uses to be integrated in our SDK (for example: add new functionalities in codecs, read/write files, develop sample applications for clients);
Program for multi-task hardware (multi-core computing);
Maintain and improve the quality of existing code (refactoring);
Do research on new technologies;
Participate in team code reviews;
Participate actively in different projects.
Qualifications
Bachelor's degree student in Software Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering with computer option or a strong interest in object-oriented programming;
Having completed a minimum of 30 credits and a GPA equal to or greater than 2.9/4.3 or 2.6/4.0;
Knowledge of object-oriented concepts;
Experience in software development in C++ and/or Java and/or JavaScript in a Windows or Linux environment;
Knowledge of development tools Visual studio, GIT, Bitbucket and JIRA
Knowledge in Agile and Scrum practices (XP, TDD).

Position Summary:
The hardware group concentrates on the design and validation of video cards and programmable circuits. This dynamic team welcomes its students by providing them with challenges that meet their needs.
Responsibilities
Assist the hardware engineers with product development;
Research new components and validate prototypes;
Participate in the electrical design of video cards (drawings);
Participate in the design and simulation of FPGAs (VHDL);
Debug and validate electronic boards and circuits;
Assists with the development of PCB’s using CAD.
Qualifications
Bachelor’s degree student in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science or Micro-electronics;
Having completed a minimum of 60 credits and a GPA equal to or greater than 2.9/4.3 or 2.6/4.0;
Familiar with programmable logic (FPGAs), electronic design and simulation tools for VHDL, ModelSim, Synplify), and electronic circuit debugging tools (Oscilloscope, logic analyzer, etc.).

Position Summary
The Application Engineer Internship (OEM Solutions) is a unique role as it requires a challenging mix of technical expertise in software development and a seasoned customer approach skill. You must clearly and thoroughly communicate technical details and development concepts, while being an accomplished customer service professional. You will be working closely with internationally known customers/leaders in their respective fields, who integrate Matrox technologies in their applications and devices. Under the supervision of the Technical Support Manager, you will analyze customer requirements and contribute to the development and enhancement of SDKs, including APIs, device drivers, setup packages, sample code and more. Moreover, you will work on problems of diverse scopes, where analysis of data requires evaluation of identifiable factors, while exercising your judgment within generally defined practices and policies in selecting methods for obtaining solutions.
Responsibilities
Working alongside the current OEM support team, you will be exposed to;
Developing, building and maintaining a software applications library to demonstrate the capabilities of the Matrox development platform;
Hold a registry of interactions with the clients to document the history of their problems and applied solutions;
Shadow OEM agent that will interface directly with customers, development engineers (software and hardware), Product and Project Managers and Sales Representatives on product requirements, deployment and technical issues;
Ensure that design and code are well documented;
Perform maintenance and enhancements to existing products;
Participate in setting up complex systems to reproduce customer environments.
Qualifications
Enrolled in a Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer science or other related domain;
Good experience with the Windows environment;
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills;
Well organized and meticulous;
Attention to detail with organizational skills;
Excellent written and oral communications skills.
Good knowledge of Linux operating systems;
Networking and/or digital video experience;
C++ and C # programming experience;
Knowledge of German, Chinese or Japanese will be considered an asset.
